{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310568,"nonce":"wEJIrfk/XdGlDVWoi6d9twJGI+c=","title":"Array\u003cI\u003e with I declared cross-file now wraps elements in fat pointers via lazy vtable + Placeholder fallback (commit ea32e95)","message":"`var arr:Array\u003cI\u003e = [new A(), new B()]; for (e in arr) e.name();` with `I`/`A`/`B` in separate files used to SIGSEGV. Two failures:\n\n**Failure 1 — Placeholder type for cross-file interface element.** The Let handler at `lower_array_literal` call site checks `get_interface_symbol(element_type)` to decide whether to route through the interface-wrap path. In cross-file `Array\u003cI\u003e` scenarios, `I` resolved to `TypeKind::Placeholder { name }` in this file's compile context (forward reference not materialised). `get_interface_symbol` only matched `TypeKind::Interface` so it returned None; the array literal lowered through the generic path without wrapping; raw class pointers got stored.\n\n**Failure 2 — Missing vtable when class compiled before interface.** With topo-sort ordering placing `A.hx` before `I.hx`, `register_class_metadata` for A saw `implements I` as a Placeholder TypeId, never resolved I to its symbol, and never inserted `interface_vtables[(A, I)]`. The wrap then silently bailed.\n\nFixed in `ea32e95`:\n\n1. **`get_interface_symbol` Placeholder branch** — falls back to (a) searching `interface_method_names` for a sym with that name, then (b) walking the symbol table for any `SymbolKind::Interface` symbol named that. Recovers the resolved interface SymbolId without needing the type_table to be updated.\n\n2. **`wrap_in_interface_fat_ptr` lazy vtable build** — when `interface_vtables.get((class, iface))` misses, walks `interface_method_names[iface]` and constructs the vtable from `class_method_symbols` (cross-file) or `class_method_by_name` (per-file). Inserts the built vtable so subsequent wraps stay O(1).\n\n3. **Removed `interface_vtables.contains_key` gate** at the array-literal wrap call site — the wrap function now handles the missing case internally.\n\n**How to apply:** Any `Array\u003cInterface\u003e` where the implementing classes get compiled before the interface — common when several classes implement the same interface and topo-sort places them first. Iterator-of-interface patterns, registry arrays, factory lists.\n\n**Test:** `/tmp/staticbug` minimal repro prints A/B/etc. correctly.\n\n**Open follow-up — `Reg.entries.length` typecheck false-positive.** Static-field-then-instance-field chained access (`Reg.entries.length` where `entries:Array\u003cX\u003e`) is misparsed/typechecked as a type path: `Cannot find type 'Reg.entries.length'`. Separate from this fix.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_cross_file_iface_array` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}